our shout out tonight to all the  reporters who this week were awarded  Pulitzer Prizes and for the Pulitzer  committee itself which this year chose  to honor a select group of reporters who  did not win  before I announce where they are I want  to break with tradition and offer my  sincere admiration for an entry that did  not win but that should give us all hope  for the future of journalism in this  great democracy the entry is from the  staff of the Eagle Eye student newspaper  at Marjory Stoneman Douglas High School  in parkland Florida which submitted the  obituaries of 17 coaches and classmates  who were killed during a tragic shooting  in their school in February 2018 the  eagle eyes submission stated that the  student reporters and editors had to  quote put aside our grief and recognize  our role as both survivors journalists  and loved ones of the deceased end quote  these budding journalists remind us of  the media's unwavering commitment to  bearing witness even in the most  wrenching of circumstances in service to  a nation whose very existence depends on  a free and dedicated press there is hope  in their example even as security  threats to journalists are greater than  ever and there is hope even if some  wrongly degrade the media as the enemy  of the very democracy it serves of  course the press will endure because as  the founding fathers knew well there can  be no democracy without it  that is something Rebecca Smith wendy  Winters  robbed hyacinth Gerald Fishman and John  McNamara understood too they understood  it when they went to work last June at  the Capitol Gazette in Annapolis  Maryland and were gunned down by a  madman who opened fire in their newsroom  it is what Jamal could show he  understood as well when he bravely wrote  truth to power at the Washington Post  before being murdered in October 2018  inside the Saudi consulate in Turkey in  all 63 professional journalists  worldwide were killed this year  according to reporters without borders  that is a 15% increase in journalists  who lost their lives for simply trying  to do their jobs and their spirit this  year's winning work reflects yet again a  steely resolve in upholding the highest  principles and ideals of this noble  profession a sobering and important  reminder that's our program for this  week we'll see you back here again next  week good night  you
 

